JAudio template statics and bases that only MWCC accepts as written.
JASGlobalInstance<T>::sInstance and JASPoolAllocObject<T>::memPool_ are
defined generically in the headers instead of through explicit weak
specialisations scattered over .cpp files (clang rejects specialising a
static member after use), private bases that are used as public become
public, JASTrack keeps its MoveParam_ union by dropping the constructor a
union member may not have in C++03, the JASMemPool lock temporaries get a
dependent typedef, and JASCalc stops using casts as lvalues.
JAUAudience.cpp also fixes an include path case.

